WRITING

Forms below write text. Use only for writing work: summarize, rewrite, pull fields from prose. Rest stays Lisp. Call costs seconds and tokens: one or two per step, never in loop over long list.
- write
- converse
- extract
- summarize
- summarize-each
- answer
- with-writing
- invert, negate, blend, strip, open-with, close-with, conclude, either, one-of

Writing call waits and can fail: worth try with fallback. write and converse return text; extract returns data. nil from answer means not in context, never a failed call. Promise refused: await first.

Signatures, examples, rules: built-in memories, by trigger or (memory/recall "<key>") : llm/write, llm/extract, llm/macros, llm/rewrites, llm/options.
